    ns1:description "To disassemble the chair, place it upside down on a soft and flat surface, then use the Allen key to loosen and remove all screws securing the backrest to the seat before carefully separating the backrest. Next, remove the screws attaching each leg to the seat and detach the legs one by one. Keep all screws and small parts together to avoid loss during storage or transport, and store the chair components in a dry and safe place to prevent damage."^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:name "Chair Disassembly For Manufacturing"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:comment "Assembly instruction of Chair Disassembly For Manufacturing with ID 75yGiZ" ;
    pdto:hasTargetAudience "Professional"^^xsd:string .

<https://cir4fun.eu/data#disposalinstruction_KRRmcj> a pdto:DisposalInstruction ;
    rdfs:label "disposalInstruction_End-of-Life_Disposal_KRRmcj" ;
    ns1:description "At the end of the chair’s service life, disassemble all components and separate the materials such as metal, plastic, wood, and fabric where applicable. Dispose of each material according to local recycling and waste management regulations. Reusable parts should be recovered whenever possible, and damaged or non-recyclable components must be disposed of through an authorized waste collection facility. Do not dispose of the chair in natural environments or with uncontrolled household waste."^^xsd:string ;
    ns1:name "End-of-Life Disposal"^^xsd:string ;
    rdfs:comment "Disposal instruction of End-of-Life Disposal with ID KRRmcj" .

